  "body": "#1035: #574 made every built-in mill post state its spindle stopped (M5; MOTOFF on Mazak) after a touch probe's tool change and length offset, before its first move. A control whose tool change leaves the spindle turning (a same-tool continuation, a manual change) then still brings the probe to the part stopped. `doosan-dnm.cps` (#614) came after #574. Its `startPreamble` skipped S/M3 for a section with a stated speed of 0 but wrote no M5, and `probe_spindle_stop.rs`'s `MILL_POSTS` left it out.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0, PROCESS_VERSION 17; merged with upstream main at a0891091.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`: after the tool change, the G43 and the skipped spindle start, a section with a stated speed of 0 writes `M5`, before the first move. A cutting section is unchanged.\n- `crates/app/tests/probe_spindle_stop.rs`: `(\"doosan-dnm\", \"M5\")` joins `MILL_POSTS`, so both of its tests cover the post:\n  - `a_probe_section_stops_its_spindle_after_the_tool_change_on_every_mill_post`\n  - `a_cutting_section_states_no_spindle_stop_before_its_first_move`\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1035-doosan-probe-m5.md`.\n\n**Overlap with #1034** (#995, @mkinney, open draft): it edits the same `startPreamble`. It adds a `touchProbe` variable at the function's top line and gates the coolant line.\n- This PR writes its condition inline after the spindle block instead (`spindleWait && !(sRpm > 0)`). A zero-speed section never clears `spindleWait`, so the condition still holds at that point.\n- Neither PR touches the other's lines. A trial merge of this branch with #1034's head 5d8b71e2 is clean.\n- I did not stack on #1034: it carries a breaking `feat(post)!` (Air coolant, #869) and merges at the next cut, which would hold this P2 fix until then.\n\n## How it was tested\n\n- Pinning test: `probe_spindle_stop::a_probe_section_stops_its_spindle_after_the_tool_change_on_every_mill_post`. It fails on main with \"doosan-dnm: no M5 between the tool change and the first move\" and passes with the fix. Its cutting-section twin stays green for doosan-dnm.\n- Every app suite that posts through `doosan-dnm` or probes, run by hand, all green: `conformance`, `doosan_dnm_post`, `fourth_axis_pose`, `post_unit_word`, `golden_cl`, and the 12 `probe_*` suites.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post`: 66 passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, but for a `.cps`-only change it plans almost nothing (#923). That is why the suites above were run by hand.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No snapshot PNG touched. No posted golden changes (none probes on doosan-dnm).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Not run on a Doosan control.\n- The fix is pinned with the generic `3axis-vmc.mch`, as the other posts in `probe_spindle_stop` are, not with a Doosan machine file.\n\nChangelog: Doosan DNM post: a touch probe section states its spindle stopped (M5) before its first move, like the other mill posts (#1035)\n\nEffort: high (the issue's label: posted G-code is under the safety floor). Not escalated.\n\nFixes #1035\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
